        "original_id": "99f57ad1-7eaf-528d-aa6e-3ec15a0cd7ec",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Geoffrey Cheshire, Leonard Cheshire\n- Roles: father, war hero, founder, Royal Air Force pilot, philanthropist\n- Organizations: Cheshire Foundation Homes for the Sick, Royal Air Force\n- Events: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Geoffrey Cheshire was the father of Leonard Cheshire.\n- Leonard Cheshire was born on 7 September 1917 and died on 31 July 1992.\n- Leonard Cheshire was an English war hero and a highly decorated World War II Royal Air Force pilot.\n- Leonard Cheshire held the titles VC and Baron Cheshire.\n- Leonard Cheshire founded the Cheshire Foundation Homes for the Sick.\n- Leonard Cheshire was also a philanthropist.",
